Z||000016||bHooper||08-12-2001||07:37 PM||||hey people... our mystery guest is concerned about handleing... lets face it, a heavy ass v8 (like a northstar or such)= bad handleing and evil weight distribution.<P>i'm sure there are many v-8's that don't weigh all that much (Archie's the expert), but the n* weghs a ton.  i've driven one and, while i liked the power, i hated the handleing.<P>so suspension first... i think there is a lot to be had our of the pre-88 cars.  you can tweak the heck out of them, and the Held upgrades may be the best way to do it.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000017||TwisT||08-12-2001||08:24 PM||||Ahmen to Archie on this one.  Listen carefully to the words of a man who has been making Fieros "Super Cars" practically since the first day the Fiero was made available to the public.  <P>Ahmen to experience.  Ahmen to knowledge.  Ahmen to Archie!<P>Remember...  Knowledge is NOT power.  USING IT IS!!!<P>BTW C5VETTE...  Your budget ALLOWS you to do it right the first time.  Take the time to investigate your options thoroughly before diving in.  <P>Wait...  what am I talking about.  With your budget,  what the hell!!!  EXPERIEMENT!!!  lol....<P>Brett  <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/italbanner3.JPG"> <P>...Website coming soon!||||reg||1
