Z||000023||C5Vette||08-12-2001||10:14 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>Did ya ever get the feeling that you've been had by the C5vette person ??? Rather unusal that this person starts a string and ya never see another post. Not much info in the profile either????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR> Wow! man you need to slow down, I posted this then went to work, I got home 2 hours ago and just now turned on the comp (damn 15 hour shifts). BTW I love your car but its not 100% what I'm looking for.<P> Thank you for all the suggestions.<P> Once I sell the Vette I'm going to buy a 88GT 5 speed T-Top and have Archie install a hot LT-1 and chop its top, then get some 17" wheels and Koni suspension big breaks AND... I need more suggestions!!<P> I will keep you posted.<P><p>[This message has been edited by C5Vette (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||California Kid||08-12-2001||10:42 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by C5Vette:<BR>[B]  <P> I will keep you posted.<P>Hey......You are real!!! Didn't mean to offend you. Wish you all the luck on your project, the final result is going to blow you away!<P>The guy who owned/started the project on my car was and is also a C5 owner. He has regreted selling me the car since day one, claims he's never owned a car that was so much fun. We still stay in touch even though 3 years have passed. Just so you have some idea what you're in for, he raced for Porsche during 60's/70's, and proved that the 88 Fiero GT with the right modifications can whip any production car up to $6 figures(I'm talkin' "all around" competition, not just drag racing).<P>Again, No Flame implied or intended, was just starting to wonder.<P>Welcome to the Forum.<BR>Tom <P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000025||artherd||08-13-2001||12:31 AM||||Hi C5, welcome to the fourm!<P>The new vettes are nice, but as you said; hardly origional.   You'll find fiero owners can't leave their cars alone, one of the rarest fieros you will see is actually a bone stock car ;)  We've all got our own take on how we'd do our 'blue sky' car, and here's mine! :)<P>wow. $50k to work with :)<P>Ok, what you need to do is pay me to build your car, grin :)<P>Start with the Lotus/Mercury-Marine Crovette LT5 4-cam V8. (425bhp stock...)<BR>This will run us ~$15,000.<P>We will use a Quartermaster twin-plate clutch (Tom aka California Kid has one.)<P>Engine Swap will be done by Archie (if he's willing.) $5-8k ? ,est.<P>(option 2 here, an Audi FWD 6-speed instead of teh stock 5-speed. more $)<P>Held Motorsports will provide a complete tubular coil over suspension with a fabricated tubular rear cradle using inboard (F1/Indycar style) shocks. <P>Also will provide 13" front and rear brakes with 4-piston Wilwoods.<BR>$10,000.+<P><BR>We will start with a low-mileage 88 with T-tops, and if you can fit in the car, I'd recomend having Archie 'chop' the top.<BR>$13k for car with chopped top.<P>Miscalenous interior setups are of course even more subjective, you'll have to let me know your tastes :)<P>This was fun, thanks for letting me streach a bit.  I'm going to be doing a similar car soon, but on a much smaller scale (4-cam Northstar V8, stock 5-speed, twinplate clutch, and a big surprise in the brakes :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000026||Slammed Fiero||08-13-2001||01:10 AM||||Zr1's were rated at 375hp until 93 when they were bumped to 405hp.<P>The motor is heavy and parts are hard to come by. We had one for 3yrs , great highway car...<P>Keep in mind an Lt1 vette would out corner a ZR1 , due to the weight.<P>Go LS1 , wanna spend more money?? I saw a TWM induction setup on an LS1 , looked like webbers.<P>Throw out any idea of mounting the motor horizontally.<P><BR>Get a c5 rear mount transaxle , IT can be mounted directly to the Engine , my dad is working on a mid engine V8 Corvair with this setup. Kennedy Engineering can build you an adaptor quite cheaply. This is the expensive route<P>OR<P>this is cheaper<P>Get a Porsche Transaxle , they  can handle the power. Anything to 94 will be a 5spd unit. Skip the Hewland or Zf gear boxes...too quirky.<P>Make sure your 911 Gear box has a LSD , look for a car optioned with a 40% LSD. a wee bit hard to find , but you will be happier with it. Turbo cars have it , Special order RS's have a close ratio good luck , they only ever buil 105 RS's with the close ratio unit.<P>Held / Ryane Suspension (No comment , join the Fiero racing list and ask some of them what they think of it. There are some well know racers who went with it and changed. There are some street guys who don't like it either. What do you wanna do , look fancy , or be functional??<P><BR>Brakes... Again ... skip the pre cut kits. Why bother with them anyway?? with all the power you want , you will want heavier rear spindles , hubs ect, ie not 5x100.  Keep the bolt pattern the same all around , keeps life simple.<P><BR>I would custom build a Cross member for the front of the car , and use Vette parts and spindles.<P>OR , I would make the car a Tub..IE chop off the bad parts of the suspension ..ie and the front and back of the car. You can still get schematics / blueprints for Tube frame Fiero's. Copy an IMSA Huffaker body , the Tub route will enable you to use better offsets on the wheels , IE make the car lower. I have always thought the imsa kit ..even on lowered cars looked like it sat high<P>Mount your fuel cell up front.. as low as you can. Put a carpeted tray or "bucket" over the fuel cell to finish off the front.<P><BR>Basically , to build a Fiero that will really whoop a super car , you will have to spend a lot... There supercars for a reason. You may be able to beat them in a straight line, But I have driven 1900lbs-2100lbs  88's with the mods everyone has mentioned above ..big brakes , tubular suspension ect. It was about as fast as most track / street 911.<P>A lot of people may want to think this is easy.. But in actuality , your going to be cutting a lot of what the Fiero is and tossing it. <P>If you want a supercar killer , you would have been better off keeping the vette.<P><BR>Sorry , flame suit on.<P>JM <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Slammed Fiero||08-13-2001||01:14 AM||||Just to clarify , the term supercar, is related to cars like a Saleen s7 , and Mac F1. I don't care what kind of fancy suspension you bolt on , your gonan get spanked. The cars are purpose built.<P>I personally like archies idea with the exception of a few things. If you wanna go hunt supercars , your gonna need to do a lot of work.<P>Not ragging on the Fiero.. or I wouldn't have put all that money into my car.<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000028||JayUSA77||08-13-2001||02:53 AM||||hey slammed fiero i have a question can you send your email to me at jayusa77@home.com i need more info on porshea transaxles.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000029||LT1 Chop Top||08-13-2001||04:52 AM||||C5,<P><BR>You will LOVE it!<P>I went to a show and shine last Friday night and wasn't participating (got there really late), but I parked next to the Corvette section....nose to nose with a new C5 that was nearly the same blue color.  I went looking at the cars and came back and there was a crowd around my car, ignoring the C5's.  It was pretty cool, and the Blue C5 owner was even complimentary (a rare thing).  It is nice to have such a unique car (one of 5 Fiero Chop's in existence, they only Fastback model, and the only one that is 'on the road' to my knowledge) that costs WAY less than a C5 and can certainly keep up with them!  Good Luck! ||||reg||1
Z||000030||AusFiero||08-13-2001||04:56 AM||||Well one of my body kits would be a good start without eating into the budget much at all  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And it will still be unique and also still be a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000031||LT1 Chop Top||08-13-2001||04:57 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f2_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000032||artherd||08-13-2001||07:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Just to clarify , the term supercar, is related to cars like a Saleen s7 , and Mac F1. I don't care what kind of fancy suspension you bolt on , your gonan get spanked. The cars are purpose built.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agreed.   There's a reason they cost $quarter-mil and above.   Heck, at .5mil a Ferrari F50 is a downright bargin (they say you pay for just the engine, and they throw the rest of the car in for free.)<P>That said, a Fiero can be made to run with them in a mountian road cruise, if not in an all-out track situation.<P>PS: Slammed, I want to meet you one day, I smell a grudge match of personal styles coming, I look forward to swapping cars for a few laps :)<P>Love to hear more about your C5 tranny project, custom bellhousing? <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
