Z||000037||87FieroGTx||08-14-2001||01:45 AM|||| I think he needs to sell the Corvette to get the 50k.<P> My suggestion would be<P> Get the Custom Tubular frame from Warlock designes, It has all suspension parts to pull 1.5g and 12" brakes $10,000<P> Longitudinal mounted Turbocharged hot LS-1 V8 forged bottom end (650hp) Hook it up to a Porsche 930/pantera Trans good for up to 700hp there's another $15,000<P> Your choice of body kits for 10,000 (My friend just did a Diablo SE and it looks just like the real thing intill you see/hear the 3.8 V6.<P> Nice leather interior $5,000 at most.<P> Get a fully optioned Fiero parts car $1,000<P> You could do all this at home with minimal knowledge. It took Sam and I  75 man hours to complete his Diablo (Body, paint, Interior, Brakes and Wheels)<P> The kit bodie, tube frame, V8 and trans will bring the weight up to around 3,000lbs<BR>But with 650hp you will be doing 4 sec 0-60s, 11's in the 1/4 mile and 1.5 on the skidpad.<P> ~~~~~~~~~~~~OR~~~~~~~~~~~~~<P> Get a 88 GT<P> Chop the top $3,000<BR> Get a (HOT) GNX Turbo 3.8 450hp $10,000<BR> Or a Intercooled 3.8s/c 350hp $5,000<BR> 17" Light weight Magnesium wheels with Perellie P 0's $1,000<BR> Full Koni suspension $1,100<BR> Stage 2 body kit $1,000  ????????????<BR> <BR> This setup should give you mid 12's in the 1/4   4.5  0-60   1.1 skidpad||||reg||1
Z||000038||FieroKyle||08-14-2001||02:21 AM||||Well, Archie has to be happy, he is gonna make 40K off this guy. HaHa.<BR>Wow? a super Fiero??? Stick a V-8 in it and new suspension.<BR>The 350's only wiegh 80 lbs more. To spend all 50k in a Fiero, well you won't have a Fiero, you will have a whole new car. Its probably gonna be actually hard to spend it all on a Fiero. Thats interior, exterior, engine, suspension, add-ons, rims, ect.... Good luck buddy, when done make sure you bring it to the shows.||||reg||1
